[s0l0!-header][h1]setInterval[/h1][/s0l0!-header] 

The [b]setInterval()[/b] method calls a function or evaluates an expression at specified intervals (in milliseconds).
It will continue calling the function until [b]clearInterval()[/b] is called or the window is closed.

[s0l0!-header][b]For example:[/b][/s0l0!-header] [code format="js" codeId="704"]function myAlert() {
   alert("Hi");
}
[b]setInterval(myAlert, 3000);[/b][/code]
This will call the myAlert function every 3 seconds (1000 ms = 1 second).
[note]Write the [b]name [/b]of the function without parentheses when passing it into the [b]setInterval [/b]method. [/note]

